{"title":"Career Roadmap · Academic Coordinator","role":"Academic Coordinator","summary":"An Academic Coordinator supports the planning, implementation, monitoring and continuous improvement of academic activities within a school, college, coaching organization or educational institution.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Ed (Bachelor of Education)","Course":"B.Ed - Subject Pedagogy (Science / Maths / Social Studies / Languages / Commerce)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Academic Coordinator supports the planning, implementation, monitoring and continuous improvement of academic activities within a school, college, coaching organization or educational institution."},{"type":"p","text":"The role connects:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teachers"},{"text":"Students"},{"text":"Academic leadership"},{"text":"Parents"},{"text":"School administration"},{"text":"Curriculum teams"},{"text":"Assessment teams"},{"text":"Management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic planning"},{"text":"Timetable coordination"},{"text":"Teacher coordination"},{"text":"Curriculum implementation"},{"text":"Lesson-plan monitoring"},{"text":"Assessment planning"},{"text":"Examination coordination"},{"text":"Student performance tracking"},{"text":"Teacher training"},{"text":"Academic documentation"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Educational technology adoption"},{"text":"Academic quality improvement"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Ed graduate, the most natural pathway is generally:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Teacher","Experienced Teacher","Academic Lead/Subject Coordinator","Academic Coordinator"]},{"type":"note","label":"Career-positioning note","text":"Academic Coordinator is usually an experience-based education-management role, rather than a direct entry-level position immediately after B.Ed. Some schools may appoint junior a